      feat(scala): support typed implicit lambda params and $DECL metavariable
      
      Inline semgrep-ext.js into grammar.js, removing the common/ split.
      
      Add two new grammar extensions:
      
      1. Fix lambda_expression to support the ResultExpr/BlockResult form from
         the Scala 2.13 and 3.4 specs (§6.23):
      
           { implicit request: Request[AnyContent] => body }
      
         The upstream grammar used seq(optional("implicit"), $._identifier),
         which dropped 'implicit' silently and couldn't accommodate a type
         annotation. Split into an explicit 'implicit' branch with optional
         type and a plain identifier branch to avoid LR conflicts. A patch for
         upstream tree-sitter-scala is in 0001-fix-lambda-typed-implicit-parameter.patch.
      
      2. Add semgrep_val_or_var_definition to support patterns of the form
      
           $DECL $NAME = expr
      
         where the val/var keyword is abstracted by a metavariable. Wired into
         _definition so it is available in both class bodies and blocks.
      
      Add a test in semgrep_real_patterns.txt for a hardcoded-secret-in-JWT
      pattern that exercises both extensions together.
